 "requested_at": "2026-11-11T15:58:51.006616Z",
 "text": "The clause is not enforceable. Section 106 of the *Residential Tenancies Act, 2006* limits what a landlord may apply a rent deposit to, and it does not allow the deposit to cover unpaid utilities or cleaning costs. The landlord would need to pursue those amounts separately, for example by applying to the Landlord and Tenant Board. The tenant also remains entitled to the deposit, including any interest owed under the Act, less any proper rent arrears.\n\nI'm working from memory of the Act, so please check the current text of s. 106 on e-Laws (ontario.ca/laws) before relying on this.\n\nVerdict: not enforceable\nSection: 106",
